//  ccwrap llibcxx03: <future> for Open Watcom. promise<T> / future<T> /
//  shared_future<T> over a heap shared state synchronized with the REAL
//  <mutex> + <condition_variable> (so a producer thread can hand a value to a
//  consumer thread). T must be default-constructible (the value is stored by
//  value). async() is NOT provided (its return type needs decltype/result_of).
//  packaged_task<R(Args)> IS provided (arity 0..2, non-void R): its signature gives
//  R explicitly, so the callable is stored in a function<> and the result routed
//  through a promise<R>. Exception propagation works through
//  promise::set_exception(exception_ptr) -> get() rethrows it (the <exception> subset
//  is enough; note it preserves what() but not the exact type for a caught
//  _CCW_STD::exception). A promise abandoned without a value makes get() throw
//  future_error(broken_promise). future_errc / launch / future_category /
//  make_error_code and future_error::code() are provided.
